This recipe (scripts, tools and documents) is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. See LICENSE.

It contains no model weights and no third-party source code. chat/chat_template.jinja is ours, written to render
what DeepSeek's reference encoding renders. Its kit/ folder holds compiled code: our own kernels, TensorFold's EXL3
kernels with our additions, PyTorch's attention kernel for the vision tower, unmodified, and libtfgrammar, the
grammar library built from xgrammar, in binary form; kit/KIT-LICENSES.md gives each file's source and license, and
kit/LICENSES/ and kit/grammar/ hold the license texts. It runs, or was built with reference to, the third-party work
below. ATTRIBUTION.md says what was taken from each one and how.

TensorFold
  Copyright 2026 TensorFold contributors. Apache License 2.0 from TensorFold 0.6.0; code written before 0.6.0
  keeps its MIT notice (MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 TensorFold contributors).
  https://github.com/ashhart/TensorFold
  The serving engine. Our engine for this model is branch deepseek-v41-zig-tp2 of our fork
  (https://github.com/bertholomus/TensorFold), which keeps TensorFold's LICENSE and upstream license texts, lists the
  upstream files it changes in its NOTICE and every outside source in its ATTRIBUTION.md.
  The branch carries pull requests to our fork by Lucas Peters (#4), lepetitprince716-prog (#18), Manrique (#26,
  and #28 and #29 ported), Scott Woolsey Biggart (#30), mrsergiopascal (#31) and Blackwellboy (#33 and #34), and,
