  0.6.0 keeps its MIT notice, kit/LICENSES/TensorFold-MIT.txt (TensorFold's LICENSES/MIT.txt, unmodified).

DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017 and DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash
  Copyright (c) 2023 DeepSeek. MIT License (inference code and weights).
  https://huggingface.co/deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017
  https://huggingface.co/deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash
  The model. Its inference code and tech report were read for the model math. No code was copied. Its reference
  encoding (encoding.py) is what chat/chat_template.jinja renders and what our exact-chat check compares against; no
  code was copied. The original shards 47 and 48 (Engram tables) are loaded at run time and not included here. The
  gates' bias_vl tensors are made into kit/vision/gate_bias_vl.safetensors by kit/tools/make_bias_vl.py; git does not
  hold that file.

DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017-EXL3-2.5bpw
  EXL3 quantization by BertholomusAI. MIT License, inherited from the base model.
  https://huggingface.co/bertholomus/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017-EXL3-2.5bpw
  The weights the engine serves since v0.7.0. Not included here. tools/serving_1017.py adds six of its tensors under
  the engine's names and types, and the chat template, to a download of it. Made with ExLlamaV3's converter and
  Fabiano Anemone's DeepSeek-V4 support for it (https://github.com/turboderp-org/exllamav3/pull/449, MIT).

DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-EXL3-2.9bpw
